  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Jobs",
     "texto": [
      "To ask what someone does for work: **Was bist du von Beruf?** (with «Sie»: **Was sind Sie von Beruf?**).",
      "You answer **without an article**: **Ich bin Lehrer** (I am a teacher).",
      "The feminine adds **-in**: Lehrer → **Lehrerin**, Student → **Studentin**. Sometimes the vowel changes: Arzt → **Ärztin**.",
      "To negate a noun, use **kein**, not «nicht»: **Sie sind keine Studenten** (they are not students)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The regular present tense",
     "texto": [
      "Almost all verbs are conjugated the same way: you remove **-en** and add the endings. The endings for **wir** and **sie/Sie** are the same as the infinitive.",
      "If the stem ends in -t or -d, add an **e** so it can be pronounced: **du arbeitest**, **er arbeitet**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
